  "narrative": "Capital is flowing predominantly into the Energy sector, which has outperformed the SPY by 10.1% over the past month. This suggests a strong investor preference for energy stocks, possibly driven by favorable commodity prices or geopolitical factors affecting supply. Materials and Financials are also seeing significant inflows, outperforming the SPY by 4.6% and 3.2%, respectively, indicating a broader interest in sectors sensitive to economic cycles and interest rates.\n\nThe macroeconomic backdrop shows a decrease in the fed funds rate by 16% year-over-year, which could be stimulating investment in interest-sensitive sectors like Financials. Meanwhile, the 10-year Treasury yield has increased slightly by 2% year-over-year, suggesting moderate inflation expectations. The high-yield spread has narrowed by 31%, indicating reduced credit risk perceptions, which might be encouraging investment in riskier assets.\n\nThe VIX is down 49% year-over-year, signaling decreased market volatility and potentially boosting investor confidence. However, options data shows bearish sentiment in technology stocks like AMD and GOOGL, suggesting caution in this sector despite its recent 2.0% outperformance. Conversely, bullish options activity in companies like ABBV and GS indicates investor optimism in healthcare and financial services. Watch for changes in macroeconomic indicators, particularly interest rates and credit spreads, as they could shift capital flows and investor sentiment.",
